        "id": "p29-q80-query",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "How many points on the following composite functions have a horizontal tangent?",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p29-q80-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "$y=f(g(x))$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "1 point; $g'(x)=0$ once and $g(x)>1$.",
              "worked": "By the chain rule, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}f(g(x))=f'(g(x))g'(x)$. The graph shows $g'(x)=0$ once. Since $f$ has its stationary point at input $1$ and $g(x)>1$ for finite $x$, $f'(g(x))$ is never zero. Hence there is $\\boxed{1}$ point.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 58
          },
          {
            "id": "p29-q80-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$y=g(f(x))$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "3 points; $f'(x)=0$ once and $f(x)=1$ twice.",
              "worked": "By the chain rule, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}g(f(x))=g'(f(x))f'(x)$. The graph shows $f'(x)=0$ at its vertex. Also, $g'$ is zero at input $1$, and $f(x)=1$ at two points, one on each side of its vertex. These give three distinct points, so the answer is $\\boxed{3}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 66
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
